Network-Diagnostic Overview

Full-Network-Diagnostic.ps1 
What it does: Audits the active adapter interface, verifies drivers, validates network configurations, and provides color-coded fix recommendations.

Get-ActiveConnection.ps1 
What it does: Maps active network connections directly to the application process using them and opens a searchable GUI table (Out-GridView).

Get-NetworkProfile.ps1 
What it does: Tracks connection SSIDs, protocol binding (IPv4/IPv6), and network category types (Public vs. Private) to rule out firewall blocking.

Get-NetworkSummary.ps1
What it does: Extracts local IP addresses, the Default Gateway, external public IP routing, and real-time data bandwidth usage (in MB).

Triage-connection.ps1 
What it does: Tests target latency layers (Router ➔ DNS ➔ WAN Internet ➔ Servers) and parses exact native hardware/timeout error codes when pings
fail.

 Quick Tips:
Elevated Rights. Run scripts inside an Administrator PowerShell session to guarantee full access to native WMI/CIM network properties.
Includes an integrated terminal pause, ensuring the CLI output interface remains visible until you press Enter.
